  "note": "A passage through lines (GSP 1947 Inf Div in Battle s20 pp 93-96): an incoming Bde attacks through a Bde in contact, which stays in posn and supports it until its fires are masked (para 1 p 93). The attack is the Bde attack two up (GSP s19 para 12 d p 86: 1100-1500 m by night from a brigaded FUP; the FUP 1000-1200 m from the Obj, IBB p 201, IC p 333), its FUP just forward of the holding Bns' FDL. Co-ordinated by the two Comds (para 4 pp 93-94): the areas for the passage and guides, priorities on the routes (the passing formation has priority, para 5), the time responsibility for the zone passes (at or before the time of attack, para 6 pp 94-95: the Battle Handover Line along the holding FDL), the fire the holding formation gives (normally its indirect fire only, para 7 a p 95) and its admin support. The holding formation clears and marks the lanes through its own minefields (para 10 c p 96): a lane per assault Bn with a passage point and guides at its home end (the places E); a contact point between the two Bde HQs. The passing Bde moves by night from its rear posns, timed to attack at the right time without moving into a forward assembly area (para 8 p 95). Armour passing an infantry formation does so within one unit's boundaries (para 9 p 96).",
